id: pm-swarm-9bks
title: Bound coverage reporter memory on Node 26 after a passing source suite
description: "Prior-head PR 65 CI run https://github.com/unbraind/pm-swarm/actions/runs/42782833349 passed 1189 source tests on Node 26.13.0, then c8 exhausted its approximately 4 GiB V8 heap while generating reports. Node 22 passed. Investigate report aggregation memory and certify the full unchanged 100 percent four-dimension gate on Node 22 and Node 26 without reducing scope, tests or thresholds. This resource issue is separate from the round-five correctness findings."
type: Issue
status: in_progress
priority: 2
tags[4]: ci,coverage,"gh:unbraind/pm-swarm#65",performance
created_at: "2026-11-10T08:52:59.206Z"
updated_at: "2026-11-15T21:11:40.343Z"
author: codex-agent
comments[8]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-10T16:17:09.265Z",codex-agent,"Final scoped PR 65 continuation explicitly authorizes fixing the observed CI failure. Current head 7e59834 test (26), run 42814446970, passed all 1198 source tests then c8 exhausted its approximately 4 GiB heap during report aggregation; test (22) passed. Installed c8 12 already provides --merge-async: its synchronous loader retains every raw process report before filtering, whereas the asynchronous merger reads, filters and merges one report at a time. Enable that supported streaming mode without changing source/test scope, thresholds, worker count or the production heap cap. A synthetic 125-dump corpus with large excluded vendor coverage and an actually measured authored source will exercise the real reporter under a 64 MiB heap, failing when the flag is reverted. No dependency or workflow change is required."
  "2026-11-10T16:41:26.155Z",codex-agent,"Implemented the observed Node 26 CI failure fix with c8's supported --merge-async mode. No larger production heap, dependency change, coverage exclusion or threshold reduction. Real reporter stress: 125 large raw process dumps plus measured authored source pass within a 64 MiB reporter heap and retain 100 percent of all four dimensions. Removing only --merge-async reproduces heap out of memory and the regression exits 1; restoring the flag passes. The pinned linked stress command passes 1/1; it also passes within the 471/471 importer group. Prior-head CI test (22) is successful; test (26) passed 1198 source tests and failed only during synchronous report aggregation. New Node 26 final-head CI certification remains pending."
  "2026-11-10T17:16:16.060Z",codex-agent,"Final implementation 05b0023: real incremental reporter stress passes 1/1 on Node 26.13.0 (exact failed CI runtime), with the reporter constrained to 64 MiB and all authored fixture coverage dimensions at 100 percent. It also passes on Node 24.19.0. Removing only --merge-async reproduces heap out of memory; restoring it passes. The single bounded npm test exits 0 in 1867s with 1208/1208 tests, no failures/skips/cancellations; required importer group passes 471/471 and static checks pass. The prior Node 26 failure was report aggregation after a passing source suite, not a failing source test. Production heap, dependency pins, source scope, thresholds and worker limits are unchanged. Releasing this claim and retaining in_progress; final-head Node 22/26 release-gate certification remains for CI and orchestrator verification at https://github.com/unbraind/pm-swarm/pull/65/checks."
  "2026-11-15T20:59:12.932Z",codex-sol,"Reuse existing CI/coverage item for Fleet CI v2; companion pm-cli-website-dyhg. Required test (22), test (26), and codeql remain unchanged. CodeQL remains unfiltered. Preserve identity/private-path checks, lint, duplication, full 100% coverage, install acceptance and all docs/tracker input contracts. Deep uses one gate per Node/package-manager matrix job."
  "2026-11-15T21:00:56.006Z",codex-sol,"Typecheck and lint passed; strict YAML parse passed. Required codeql remains unfiltered. Main run 43735415781 wall: Node 22 45m08s, Node 26 59m47s. Full close-crash matrix cases 74–75/106–110/143–144 s; punctuation privacy 78–79 s. Retained four deterministic late-seed Unicode fixtures. Shared harness timers scale, product linked-test/lease budgets remain unscaled. Quick model/privacy validation is bounded locally; install acceptance and exhaustive crash matrix remain in CI. No local full-depth/coverage run."
  "2026-11-15T21:02:33.503Z",codex-sol,PR #79 is open. Identity/private-path gate reports zero violations and publish verifier passes. Local strict health fails the existing managed extension host skew; follow-up pm-swarm-ci-extension-host-skew tracks it. No dependency or repository-variable changes made. New quick PR run 43761297916 is queued; final wall time unavailable.
  "2026-11-15T21:10:54.947Z",codex-sol,"Local quick model/privacy run: 131/132 pass in 504.16 s. Sole unexpected failure: tooling contract expects original named standalone identity step; restored it unconditionally on both PR legs and removed duplicate docs-block command. Identity remains in the release gate too. Models/privacy passed: deadlock 29.02 s, home/allowed corpora 14.96/12.65 s, normalization 16.64 s, punctuation 97.04 s. Local contention makes the historical hosted full punctuation 78–79 s incomparable. Retesting only the identity workflow contract."
  "2026-11-15T21:11:39.557Z",codex-sol,"Restored identity workflow contract passes on narrow retest. All other 131 tests passed in the bounded quick run. Typecheck/lint/identity/publish verifier/YAML passed. Initial hosted Node 22/26 jobs still running at final observation, so no completed PR wall time is claimed. No full local depth or separate coverage run; final quick coverage, packed installation acceptance and deep certification remain pending. No CI wait."
